From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard Spindler <richard@lateralblast.com.au>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 18:20:19 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 17/55] version: add the sphynx version to the release string

Fork-specific, not for upstream. SSH_SPHYNX is the version of the sphynx
packaging, and SSH_SNAPSHOT the date of the OpenSSH commit the tree is
built on (patches/BASE), so the release string reads for example
OpenSSH_10.6p1_snapshot20261103_hpn18.12.0_sphynx1.2.4. It is in the SSH
banner, in "ssh -V", and matched by "Match version". sphynx build refuses
to build if the sphynx tag and its own version disagree.

Regenerate this patch when the sphynx version changes.

Changelog: sphynx 0.0.3

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 version.h | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/version.h b/version.h
index 0e40da38f..64096659e 100644
--- a/version.h
+++ b/version.h
@@ -4,4 +4,6 @@
 
 #define SSH_PORTABLE	"p1"
+#define SSH_SNAPSHOT    "_snapshot20261103"
 #define SSH_HPN         "_hpn18.12.0"
-#define SSH_RELEASE	SSH_VERSION SSH_PORTABLE SSH_HPN
+#define SSH_SPHYNX      "_sphynx1.2.4"
+#define SSH_RELEASE	SSH_VERSION SSH_PORTABLE SSH_SNAPSHOT SSH_HPN SSH_SPHYNX
